 noon, the temperature registered a slight increase of ${0.7}^{∘}\\,\\text{C}.$ What was the temperature in New York at noon?" 13194139535348 17592186045417 true] [17592186097332 1074 "To determine the temperature at noon, we add the variation in temperature to the temperature in the morning of that day This gives\n\n$$\n-{2.4}^{∘}\\,\\text{C}+{0.7}^{∘}\\,\\text{C}=-{1.7}^{∘}\\,\\text{C}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the temperature in New York at noon that day was $-{1.7}^{∘}\\,\\text{C}.$" 13194139535348 17592186045417 true] [17592186097334 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139535348 17592186045417 true] [17592186097334 1071 "Jennifer is doing a science experiment in her Chemistry class. She takes a liquid with a temperature of $10.1^{∘}C$ and places it in a refrigerator. After half an hour, she removes the liquid from the refrigerator and places it on a table. She concludes that the temperature decreased by $12.7^{∘}C$.\n\nAfter half an hour, Jennifer takes the temperature of the liquid again and finds that the temperature increased by $8^{∘}C$. What is the final temperature of the liquid?" 13194139535348 17592186045417 false] [17592186097334 1071 "Jennifer is doing a science experiment in her Chemistry class. She takes a liquid with a temperature of ${10.1}^{∘}\\text{C}$ and places it in a refrigerator. After half an hour, she removes the liquid from the refrigerator and places it on a table. She concludes that the temperature decreased by ${12.7}^{∘}\\text{C}.$\n\nAfter half an hour, Jennifer takes the temperature of the liquid again and finds that the temperature increased by ${8}^{∘}\\text{C}.$ What is the final temperature of the liquid?" 13194139535348 17592186045417 true] [17592186097334 1074 "First of all, we must determine the temperature of the liquid when it was removed from the refrigerator. Since its temperature decreased by ${12.7}^{∘}\\text{C}$ compared to the initial temperature, we must subtract the variation in temperature from the initial temperature. This gives\n\n$$\n{10.1}^{∘}\\text{C}-{12.7}^{∘}\\text{C}=-{2.6}^{∘}\\text{C}.\n$$\n\nNow, we must determine the temperature of the liquid after half an hour had elapsed. Since the temperature of the liquid increased by ${8}^{∘}\\text{C}$ compared to the temperature when it was removed from the refrigerator, we add the variation in temperature to the temperature of the liquid when it was removed from the refrigerator. This gives\n\n$$\n-{2.6}^{∘}\\text{C}+{8}^{∘}\\text{C}={5.4}^{∘}\\text{C}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the final temperature of the liquid is ${5.4}^{∘}\\text{C}.$" 13194139535348 17592186045417 true] [17592186124459 1038 #edb/ref 17592186501150 13194139535348 17592186045417 true] [17592186124459 1038 #edb/ref 17592186501227 13194139535348 17592186045417 true] [17592186124460 1038 #edb/ref 17592186501201 13194139535348 17592186045417 true] [17592186124542 1038 #edb/ref 17592186501217 13194139535348 17592186045417 true] [17592186124603 1038 #edb/ref 17592186501158 13194139535348 17592186045417 true] [17592186124604 1038 #edb/ref 17592186501135 13194139535348 17592186045417 true] [17592186133278 1075 #edb/ref 17592186133279 13194139535348 17592186045417 false] [17592186133278 1075 #edb/ref 17592186133283 13194139535348 17592186045417 false] [17592186133278 1075 #edb/ref 17592186500616 13194139535348 17592186045417 true] [17592186133278 1075 #edb/ref 17592186500875 13194139535348 17592186045417 true] [17592186133278 1078 #edb/ref 17592186133281 13194139535348 17592186045417 true] [17592186133727 1038 #edb/ref 17592186501212 13194139535348 17592186045417 true] [17592186133727 1038 #edb/ref 17592186501225 13194139535348 17592186045417 true] [17592186133728 1038 #edb/ref 17592186501183 13194139535348 17592186045417 true] [17592186133743 1038 #edb/ref 17592186501159 13194139535348 17592186045417 true] [17592186133743 1038 #edb/ref 17592186501170 13194139535348 17592186045417 true] [17592186133744 1038 #edb/ref 17592186501153 13194139535348 17592186045417 true] [1759218613